1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,890
Hello everyone, this is Ria!

2
00:00:03,890 --> 00:00:07,070
It's finally July.

3
00:00:07,070 --> 00:00:08,360
July

4
00:00:08,360 --> 00:00:10,720
July has come.

5
00:00:10,720 --> 00:00:17,260
When you think of July, what comes to your mind first?

6
00:00:17,260 --> 00:00:23,840
For me, when I think of July, I immediately think of summer.

7
00:00:23,840 --> 00:00:25,090
Summer

8
00:00:25,090 --> 00:00:27,260
I think of summer.

9
00:00:27,260 --> 00:00:31,450
Very hot summer weather

10
00:00:31,450 --> 00:00:37,610
I think of Korea's very hot summer weather.

11
00:00:37,610 --> 00:00:45,440
The hottest months in Korea are July and August.

12
00:00:45,440 --> 00:00:47,850
July and August

13
00:00:47,850 --> 00:00:58,720
From this time, people start turning on air conditioners and eat a lot of shaved ice and ice cream.

14
00:00:58,720 --> 00:01:01,850
But there's something interesting.

15
00:01:01,850 --> 00:01:05,950
Right now, it's early July.

16
00:01:05,950 --> 00:01:07,520
Early July

17
00:01:07,520 --> 00:01:13,090
The word 'early' in early July means the beginning, the start.

18
00:01:13,090 --> 00:01:15,100
The start of July.

19
00:01:15,100 --> 00:01:21,760
It's early July now, but the weather in Korea is really nice.

20
00:01:21,760 --> 00:01:26,960
Usually, it gets really hot from this time.

21
00:01:26,960 --> 00:01:33,920
But strangely, the weather has been really nice these days.

22
00:01:33,920 --> 00:01:40,110
I'll show you a comment from YouTube.

23
00:01:40,110 --> 00:01:45,450
These days, the mornings and evenings are very cool.

24
00:01:45,450 --> 00:01:50,480
I wish every summer was like this.

25
00:01:50,480 --> 00:01:55,000
I really agree with this comment.

26
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:56,640
I agree.

27
00:01:56,640 --> 00:02:01,070
I wish every summer was like this.

28
00:02:01,070 --> 00:02:10,200
During the day, just turning on a fan is cool, and at night it's really the best.

29
00:02:10,200 --> 00:02:18,460
It's the perfect weather—not too hot and not too cold.

30
00:02:18,460 --> 00:02:22,670
Cool. It's cool.

31
00:02:22,670 --> 00:02:26,550
The weather these days is cool.

32
00:02:26,550 --> 00:02:31,110
In Korean, there is a word '선선하다' (seonseonhada).

33
00:02:31,110 --> 00:02:35,820
It means the weather is pleasantly cool.

34
00:02:35,820 --> 00:02:39,860
You know the word '시원하다' (siwonhada), right?

35
00:02:39,860 --> 00:02:44,620
It's a word very similar to that.

36
00:02:44,620 --> 00:02:47,190
You can use them together.

37
00:02:47,190 --> 00:02:52,230
These days, the weather is cool and refreshing.

38
00:02:52,230 --> 00:02:55,050
You can use them like this together.

39
00:02:55,050 --> 00:02:58,150
Cool and refreshing.

40
00:02:58,150 --> 00:03:04,610
So why is the Korean weather suddenly so nice?

41
00:03:04,610 --> 00:03:09,910
It was supposed to be hot, so why is it suddenly nice?

42
00:03:09,910 --> 00:03:16,480
These days, there are a lot of posts about this on Korean internet.

43
00:03:16,480 --> 00:03:21,600
I'll show you several today.

44
00:03:21,600 --> 00:03:31,820
Here, there's a title: "The reason why June these days is cool and refreshing."

45
00:03:31,820 --> 00:03:35,050
I just mentioned that, right?

46
00:03:35,050 --> 00:03:41,020
Here, they also used '시원하다' and '선선하다' together.

47
00:03:41,020 --> 00:03:43,930
It means the weather is nice.

48
00:03:43,930 --> 00:03:50,770
The title is like this, but the content is a bit difficult.

49
00:03:50,770 --> 00:03:56,820
There are some difficult words related to weather.

50
00:03:56,820 --> 00:04:04,030
But the last sentence caught my eye the most.

51
00:04:04,030 --> 00:04:06,790
It caught my eye.

52
00:04:06,790 --> 00:04:14,770
Currently, South Korea is experiencing European summer weather, haha.

53
00:04:14,770 --> 00:04:18,080
It's laughing like this.

54
00:04:18,080 --> 00:04:27,440
Lately, when I watch YouTube, a lot of weather-related videos come up in my algorithm.

55
00:04:27,440 --> 00:04:30,860
Especially about European summer weather!

56
00:04:30,860 --> 00:04:37,300
There are many videos showing how hot Europe is right now.

57
00:04:37,300 --> 00:04:39,460
Europe turned into an oven.

58
00:04:39,460 --> 00:04:41,380
European heatwave.

59
00:04:41,380 --> 00:04:44,610
These kinds of thumbnails appear.

60
00:04:44,610 --> 00:04:49,570
Here, 'heatwave' means very hot weather.

61
00:04:49,570 --> 00:04:51,130
Heatwave.

62
00:04:51,130 --> 00:04:57,630
Usually, Korean summers are very hot and humid.

63
00:04:57,630 --> 00:04:58,940
Temperature

64
00:04:58,940 --> 00:05:04,560
If you look at the temperature alone, it's similar to other countries' summers.

65
00:05:04,560 --> 00:05:10,520
But the humidity... wow, the humidity is crazy.

66
00:05:10,520 --> 00:05:13,530
The humidity is very high!

67
00:05:13,530 --> 00:05:20,290
So when you walk on the street, sometimes it feels suffocating.

68
00:05:20,290 --> 00:05:23,540
It feels suffocating like this.

69
00:05:23,540 --> 00:05:27,070
Kind of like being in a Korean sauna?

70
00:05:27,070 --> 00:05:30,920
Do you know Korean jjimjilbangs?

71
00:05:30,920 --> 00:05:37,570
When you enter a jjimjilbang, you really feel like you can't breathe.

72
00:05:37,570 --> 00:05:39,190
It's suffocating.

73
00:05:39,190 --> 00:05:43,740
I can't stay long in a jjimjilbang.

74
00:05:43,740 --> 00:05:49,430
At most 10 minutes? I don't think even 10 minutes.

75
00:05:49,430 --> 00:05:55,580
After about 5 minutes, I feel like, "I'm going out..."

76
00:05:55,580 --> 00:06:01,800
But my older sister seems to endure a bit longer.

77
00:06:01,800 --> 00:06:10,620
Anyway, every year Korean summers are very hot and humid, so it's tough.

78
00:06:10,620 --> 00:06:14,920
But the comments are really funny.

79
00:06:14,920 --> 00:06:27,420
If summer weather was originally like this, we might have developed songs like chanson and outdoor café culture.

80
00:06:27,420 --> 00:06:31,490
Isn't this comment so funny?

81
00:06:31,490 --> 00:06:35,520
Usually in Korea, July and August...

82
00:06:35,520 --> 00:06:48,410
When you think of summer in July and August, the image that comes to mind is sweating a lot and suffocating weather.

83
00:06:48,410 --> 00:06:57,980
But if the weather was like this European weather, wouldn't we also sing chanson? That's what the comment says.

84
00:06:57,980 --> 00:07:07,340
Usually, when summer comes, Korean people get a bit... grumpy.

85
00:07:07,340 --> 00:07:14,950
They say, "Ah, it's really too hot!!!" and their mood gets a bit bad.

86
00:07:14,950 --> 00:07:22,820
But with this kind of summer weather, I think we could also sing chanson.

87
00:07:22,820 --> 00:07:25,160
Outdoor café culture

88
00:07:25,160 --> 00:07:27,150
What is this?

89
00:07:27,150 --> 00:07:28,480
Outdoor

90
00:07:28,480 --> 00:07:32,240
Outdoor means a place outside.

91
00:07:32,240 --> 00:07:33,440
Roof

92
00:07:33,440 --> 00:07:35,720
There is no roof.

93
00:07:35,720 --> 00:07:39,310
No roof and you can see the sky.

94
00:07:39,310 --> 00:07:40,520
Sky

95
00:07:40,520 --> 00:07:42,560
You can see the sky.

96
00:07:42,560 --> 00:07:51,530
It's a café where you drink coffee outside, not inside.

97
00:07:51,530 --> 00:07:54,660
I mentioned this before, right?

98
00:07:54,660 --> 00:08:06,080
I like eating and drinking outside when the weather is nice, so I've been feeling good these days.

99
00:08:06,080 --> 00:08:09,980
Should I practice chanson?

100
00:08:09,980 --> 00:08:15,480
I met an American friend recently.

101
00:08:15,480 --> 00:08:16,890
American friend

102
00:08:16,890 --> 00:08:22,170
We went to a café in Gangnam, Seoul together.

103
00:08:22,170 --> 00:08:25,980
The café was so pretty!

104
00:08:25,980 --> 00:08:30,550
There was also a space where you could eat outside.

105
00:08:30,550 --> 00:08:31,970
Space.

106
00:08:31,970 --> 00:08:34,520
Totally my style.

107
00:08:34,520 --> 00:08:38,780
Honestly, it was a bit hot.

108
00:08:38,780 --> 00:08:46,030
We went during the day, not at night, so it was a bit hot.

109
00:08:46,030 --> 00:08:53,790
But even though it was hot, I wanted to eat outside.

110
00:08:53,790 --> 00:08:58,340
I wanted to feel the summer atmosphere.

111
00:08:58,340 --> 00:09:03,150
But my friend and I were on the same page.

112
00:09:03,150 --> 00:09:05,500
We were on the same page.

113
00:09:05,500 --> 00:09:10,270
My friend also wanted to eat outside.

114
00:09:10,270 --> 00:09:14,130
Of course, of course, you're my friend!!

115
00:09:14,130 --> 00:09:21,400
Because my mom and I have very different personalities.

116
00:09:21,400 --> 00:09:27,420
My mom always likes cool places no matter what.

117
00:09:27,420 --> 00:09:38,140
If I had gone to this café with my mom, she would have insisted on eating inside.

118
00:09:38,140 --> 00:09:44,640
I always jokingly say this to my mom.

119
00:09:44,640 --> 00:09:47,040
Jokingly say

120
00:09:47,040 --> 00:09:51,920
Mom, why do you have no romance?

121
00:09:51,920 --> 00:09:54,610
Why do you have no romance?

122
00:09:54,610 --> 00:09:56,410
No romance?

123
00:09:56,410 --> 00:10:00,960
Then do you know what my mom says?

124
00:10:00,960 --> 00:10:06,140
Hey, you get old too. This is how it is.

125
00:10:06,140 --> 00:10:09,090
When you get old, this is how it is.

126
00:10:09,090 --> 00:10:10,110
Funny, right?

127
00:10:10,110 --> 00:10:17,150
But I think it's really just a difference in taste.

128
00:10:17,150 --> 00:10:18,500
Difference in taste!

129
00:10:18,500 --> 00:10:20,690
What about you?

130
00:10:20,690 --> 00:10:27,130
Do you like drinking coffee outside while feeling the summer atmosphere?

131
00:10:27,130 --> 00:10:34,490
Or do you prefer drinking coffee in a cool air-conditioned place?

132
00:10:34,490 --> 00:10:40,730
The café owner asked us.

133
00:10:40,730 --> 00:10:43,670
Will you be eating inside?

134
00:10:43,670 --> 00:10:50,870
We said, "No, can we eat outside?"

135
00:10:50,870 --> 00:10:57,330
But they were very surprised and said, "Really?"

136
00:10:57,330 --> 00:11:08,030
There were many people inside the café, but only we ate outside.

137
00:11:08,030 --> 00:11:14,590
We drank drinks and talked a lot for several hours.

138
00:11:14,590 --> 00:11:19,210
Time went by very quickly.

139
00:11:19,210 --> 00:11:25,600
We sat outside for a long time on that hot day.

140
00:11:25,600 --> 00:11:28,630
It was better than I thought.

141
00:11:28,630 --> 00:11:34,980
It was a bit hot, but still bearable.

142
00:11:34,980 --> 00:11:38,320
It was bearable.

143
00:11:38,320 --> 00:11:44,310
But before going home, I looked in the mirror once.

144
00:11:44,310 --> 00:11:49,880
I looked and my face was completely red.

145
00:11:49,880 --> 00:11:51,460
It was red.

146
00:11:51,460 --> 00:11:58,350
My face was hot and red, and my skin was a mess.

147
00:11:58,350 --> 00:12:04,030
Still, it was a happy memory of early summer.

148
00:12:04,030 --> 00:12:06,680
Early summer

149
00:12:06,680 --> 00:12:10,790
Early summer means the start of summer.

150
00:12:10,790 --> 00:12:11,880
Start

151
00:12:11,880 --> 00:12:16,820
It usually refers to June to early July.

152
00:12:16,820 --> 00:12:19,140
Then midsummer!

153
00:12:19,140 --> 00:12:20,700
Midsummer

154
00:12:20,700 --> 00:12:23,100
What is midsummer?

155
00:12:23,100 --> 00:12:26,460
The hottest part of summer.

156
00:12:26,460 --> 00:12:30,530
It means the middle of summer.

157
00:12:30,530 --> 00:12:38,050
Usually, it refers to July to August after the rainy season ends in Korea.

158
00:12:38,050 --> 00:12:43,390
So what will the Korean weather be like from now on?

159
00:12:43,390 --> 00:12:50,750
Honestly, I'm not a weather expert, so I don't know well.

160
00:12:50,750 --> 00:12:58,550
I searched a bit and saw some really sad news...

161
00:12:58,550 --> 00:13:03,660
They say this cool weather will end soon.

162
00:13:03,660 --> 00:13:06,110
It will end soon.

163
00:13:06,110 --> 00:13:14,910
Starting from July, it looks like it will rain a lot from next week.

164
00:13:14,910 --> 00:13:27,490
After the rainy season ends, as always, Korea's really hot and humid summer will begin.

165
00:13:27,490 --> 00:13:40,100
So if you are living in Korea now, enjoy this cool summer night a lot!

166
00:13:40,100 --> 00:13:41,350
Okay?

167
00:13:41,350 --> 00:13:49,140
Lastly, I'll read one more Korean comment.

168
00:13:49,140 --> 00:14:04,600
I'm someone whose only exercise is night walks, so I usually don't do it in summer, but the weather is so nice these days that I've been doing it continuously.

169
00:14:04,600 --> 00:14:09,700
The air is better than in spring, it's really nice.

170
00:14:09,700 --> 00:14:11,780
No insomnia either!

171
00:14:11,780 --> 00:14:12,990
That's right.

172
00:14:12,990 --> 00:14:20,180
In Korea, when midsummer comes, you can't sleep even at night.

173
00:14:20,180 --> 00:14:23,740
This is called tropical night.

174
00:14:23,740 --> 00:14:25,400
Tropical night

175
00:14:25,400 --> 00:14:31,190
Tropical night means the weather is too hot even at night.

176
00:14:31,190 --> 00:14:46,500
This person usually doesn't take walks on summer nights because it's too hot, but these days, because the weather is nice, they keep walking.

177
00:14:46,500 --> 00:14:51,610
At the end, they said they don't have insomnia either.

178
00:14:51,610 --> 00:14:53,290
Insomnia.

179
00:14:53,290 --> 00:15:01,660
Insomnia is a state where you can't fall asleep or wake up frequently during sleep.

180
00:15:01,660 --> 00:15:04,920
I suddenly remembered something.

181
00:15:04,920 --> 00:15:11,930
I made a podcast about sleep before.

182
00:15:11,930 --> 00:15:21,310
At that time, I was in Japan and said I couldn't sleep because it was too noisy.

183
00:15:21,310 --> 00:15:28,000
But now I'm in Korea and sleeping well.

184
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:30,110
I'm really relieved.

185
00:15:30,110 --> 00:15:31,530
Relieved.

186
00:15:31,530 --> 00:15:43,050
Especially, a subscriber commented that counting numbers backward helps you sleep well.

187
00:15:43,050 --> 00:15:47,890
I tried it too and it was really good.

188
00:15:47,890 --> 00:15:54,450
Thank you to everyone who left comments then.

189
00:15:54,450 --> 00:16:01,370
Anyway, today I talked about Korea's summer weather.

190
00:16:01,370 --> 00:16:07,390
Actually, I was going to make this video a bit later.

191
00:16:07,390 --> 00:16:19,470
But before it really gets hot, I wanted to share this pleasant summer story with you all.

192
00:16:19,470 --> 00:16:21,950
From now on...

193
00:16:25,170 --> 00:16:30,980
From now on, the weather will get hotter.

194
00:16:30,980 --> 00:16:36,320
But how are people living in Europe now?

195
00:16:36,320 --> 00:16:38,650
I'm really curious.

196
00:16:38,650 --> 00:16:49,630
I saw on YouTube that French people were swimming in the river because it was so hot.

197
00:16:49,630 --> 00:16:50,820
River

198
00:16:50,820 --> 00:16:54,860
They were swimming in the river.

199
00:16:54,860 --> 00:16:58,870
How are you all doing these days?

200
00:16:58,870 --> 00:17:05,280
Please tell me a lot about your summer daily life in the comments.

201
00:17:05,280 --> 00:17:13,640
For those living in countries other than Europe, how is the summer weather in your country?

202
00:17:13,640 --> 00:17:16,320
Is it cool like Korea?

203
00:17:16,320 --> 00:17:21,380
Or is it really hot like Europe right now?

204
00:17:21,380 --> 00:17:24,290
Please tell me a lot in the comments.

205
00:17:24,290 --> 00:17:31,120
If you want to study more with me, please be sure to click this link!

206
00:17:31,120 --> 00:17:38,170
Then have a cool day today, drink lots of water...

207
00:17:38,170 --> 00:17:43,460
And we'll meet again in the next podcast! Bye :)
